// @run
// @log 7
// THE FLOOR THIS FILE PINNED IS LIFTED (silent-class-inventory D269, direction 2 of D200),
// and the name is kept so the cross-references that name it still resolve.
//
// A NARROWED `s` is still the `{tag, value}` BOX at the call: the narrow proves WHICH arm
// rides the payload, it does not re-rep the binding. `emitCallRef` had a `union`-parameter
// arm and no `variant`-parameter one, so without a floor the box went raw into a
// `(ref $uVarHeap[Circle])` slot — check-clean INVALID WASM, which is why the reject was
// added rather than the gap being called a bug.
//
// What the floor was standing in for was already written in the DIRECT twin `emitCall`,
// which is why the `function idc(x: Circle): Circle` spelling of these five lines has
// always run: `if exprUnion(arg) { struct.get $uBox 1 ; ref.cast $uVarHeap[cVi] }`. Ported
// to the value call with the slot read off the resolved `$fnsig` KEY (`sigParamSlotAt`),
// so the cast target is the row the `call_ref`'s own cast functype declares.
//
// NO LAYOUT TWIN, deliberately: `Circle` is the only `{r: i32}` in the program, so the
// disguise cannot come from a struct scan matching a same-shape row.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
const lamc = (x: Circle) => x
function m3(s: Shape) { if s is Circle { lamc(s).r } else { 0 } }
print(m3({ r: 7 }))
